---
import SymbolVisualDesk from './SymbolVisualDesk.astro';
import DeckVisualWorkspace from './DeckVisualWorkspace.astro';
import LivingCollection from './LivingCollection.astro';
const {project,cards=[],families=[]}=Astro.props;
---
<section data-chapter-panel="visual-world" hidden><p class="studio-eyebrow">Section five · The Visual World</p><h2>Your Visual Design Book</h2><details><summary>Visual direction guidance</summary><p><a href={`/studio/projects/${project.id}/visual-exchange/`}>Visual Design Exchange: prepare an artist-only snapshot</a></p><p>Before you design the cards, imagine their world.</p><p>What atmosphere, imagery and visual qualities belong to the meaning of your deck? The shared design below is a place to explore, not a print-production approval.</p><details><summary>Consider your visual language</summary><p>Color relationships, composition, recurring symbols, texture and graphic identity can connect the work without making every card identical. Keep sources and permissions with references; saving an image does not grant reproduction rights.</p></details></details><SymbolVisualDesk project={project} cards={cards} mode="direction"/><details><summary>Shared deck design</summary><p>Choose one physical size and the components you want to keep consistent before developing individual artworks. Your visual intention and references belong to this same project.</p><DeckVisualWorkspace mode="deck" project={project} cards={cards}/></details><details><summary>Your visual collection</summary><LivingCollection project={project} cards={cards} families={families} visual={true}/></details><p>Open a card to see its artwork beside its writing. The visual draft backup contains layout previews and QR choices. Use the complete private project backup for retained originals, journal sources and history; keep your own source files too.</p><button type="button" class="studio-button studio-button--secondary" data-chapter="companion">Explore The Companion</button><p class="studio-meta">This first slice does not add commissioning, artist access, production-file verification or a new media-storage service.</p></section>
<style>section h2{font:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem)/1.2 'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif}section p{line-height:1.75}details{padding:1rem 0;border-top:1px solid #cec9c1}summary{cursor:pointer}h3{margin-top:2rem}</style>

<style>section :global(.symbol-actions){position:sticky;bottom:0;z-index:2;background:#faf8f3;padding:.6rem 0;border-top:1px solid #cec9c1}</style>
